"- Object 1 Capsule\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A two-part, oblong, capsule-shaped pharmaceutical dosage form, composed of two hemispherical ends connected by a cylindrical body.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The capsule is bisected into two distinct colors: one half is solid black, and the other half is translucent orange-brown.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The capsule is approximately 1.5 to 2 centimeters in length, with a diameter of roughly 0.5 to 0.7 centimeters, typical for standard oral capsules.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The material appears to be gelatin or a similar pharmaceutical-grade polymer, with a smooth, glossy finish on both halves.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - The capsule is composed of two halves that fit together seamlessly, forming a sealed container for a solid or liquid medication inside.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One capsule is present in the image.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - The capsule is positioned horizontally and centered within the visual frame, with its longitudinal axis aligned parallel to the image's horizontal plane.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The capsule is oriented horizontally, with its rounded ends facing left and right, and its cylindrical body extending along the horizontal axis.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The two halves of the capsule are connected at their ends, forming a continuous, sealed unit with no visible external attachments or connectors.\n\n- Object 2 Printed Marking\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A numerical imprint printed on the surface of the capsule, serving as a dosage or identification mark.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The marking is printed in a light, opaque white or off-white color, contrasting against the orange-brown background of the capsule half.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The marking consists of three digits: “500”, each digit approximately 2 to 3 millimeters in height, occupying a significant portion of the orange-brown half of the capsule.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The marking is likely a printed ink or laser-etched surface treatment applied directly to the capsule shell.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - The marking is composed of three numerals (“5”, “0”, “0”) arranged sequentially in a horizontal line, with uniform spacing and alignment.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One set of printed numerals (“500”) is present.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - The marking is located on the orange-brown half of the capsule, positioned centrally along the longitudinal axis of that half.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The marking is oriented horizontally, parallel to the capsule’s longitudinal axis, and aligned with the capsule’s length.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The marking is directly printed or embossed onto the surface of the capsule shell and is not physically connected to any other object or component."